From: OpenWrt <openwrt@example.org>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 00:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: make the matchall police meter observable

tc matchall police lands on the QDMA RX TRTCM, not on a PPE meter group:
airoha_qdma_set_rx_meter() programs every RX ring of the block, while
ppe->meter[] names one group per FOE entry through AIROHA_FOE_SHAPER_ID, so
ppe/meter has no row for matchall and cannot grow one.  That difference is
the design, not a missing allocation, but until now the matchall side had no
readback at all.

Record the request in struct airoha_qdma and add qdma/rx_meter: the
requested rate, burst and unit, plus the per-ring arming read back through
TRTCM_MISC_MODE -- the same parameter airoha_qdma_set_rl_config() reads
before every write.  The token rate and bucket shift are deliberately not
printed: the driver writes them through the TRTCM parameter window and never
reads them back, so a number re-derived from the write would restate the
software record while looking like a register value.

Also state in airoha_qdma_set_rx_meter() why matchall takes no ppe->meter[]
group, so the empty ppe/meter dump is not read as a gap.

The 7.4 and 7.3 queues apply this with -F0 and no fuzz.  Not run on a device:
the per-ring mode readback still needs one capture on r38242+.

The dump reads the TRTCM parameter window, whose index and value registers
are shared with every writer of the same meter.  Give the window one
mutex per device and take it around each index/value navigation, so a
dump taken while tc re-arms the meter reads a whole parameter instead of
one half of the next one's.

Signed-off-by: OpenWrt <openwrt@example.org>
---

 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c | 249 +++++++++++++++++++++++++------
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h |  16 ++
 2 files changed, 219 insertions(+), 46 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -782,6 +782,14 @@
 }
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_DEBUG_FS
